.TH ZERODDS-MQ 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zerodds-mq \- cross-domain DDS bridge
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-mq
[\fBbridge\fR]
\fB\-\-src\-domain\fR \fIN\fR
\fB\-\-dst\-domain\fR \fIM\fR
\fB\-t\fR \fITOPIC\fR
[\fB\-\-src\-topic\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-dst\-topic\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-duration\fR \fIDUR\fR]
[\fB\-\-bidirectional\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-mq
runs two DCPS runtimes (one per DDS domain) and forwards untyped
samples from
.B \-\-src\-topic
on
.B \-\-src\-domain
to
.B \-\-dst\-topic
on
.B \-\-dst\-domain.
The encoded payload is preserved byte-for-byte.
.PP
With
.B \-\-bidirectional
samples flow both ways.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-src\-domain " " \fIID\fR
Source domain ID. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-\-dst\-domain " " \fIID\fR
Destination domain ID. Must differ from \-\-src\-domain. Default: 1.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-topic " " \fINAME\fR
Same topic name on both sides.
.TP
.BR \-\-src\-topic " " \fINAME\fR
Source topic name (overrides \-t).
.TP
.BR \-\-dst\-topic " " \fINAME\fR
Destination topic name (overrides \-t).
.TP
.BR \-\-duration " " \fIDUR\fR
Stop after duration (5, 30s, 2m, 1h). Default: until SIGINT.
.TP
.BR \-\-bidirectional
Mirror traffic in both directions.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
The base configuration file; its sibling
.IR PATH .d/
holds drop-ins. Default: the system configuration directory
.RI ( /etc/zerodds
on Linux,
.I /usr/local/etc/zerodds
on macOS).
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable;
.BI + PATH = VALUE
appends to a list.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate and print the effective configuration with the origin of every
value, then exit: 0 valid, 1 invalid value or unknown key, 2 unreadable
file, syntax error or include cycle.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
CLI parse error.
.TP
.B 3
DDS or I/O error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-spy (1),
.BR zerodds-snitch (1)
